WEBVTT

00:01.400 --> 00:04.993
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:04.994 --> 00:08.638
♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪

00:08.639 --> 00:12.097
♪ But where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪

00:12.098 --> 00:15.120
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:15.121 --> 00:18.163
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.164 --> 00:21.807
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.808 --> 00:23.412
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.413 --> 00:25.182
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:25.183 --> 00:29.634
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.844 --> 00:38.123
We now return
to Vedder Call Saul.

00:38.124 --> 00:39.879
♪ Hey, Saul ♪

00:39.880 --> 00:42.534
♪ Got into a little trouble
and I'm gonna need a lawyer ♪

00:42.535 --> 00:43.935
♪ Hey-ey ♪

00:43.936 --> 00:45.644
Okay, so tell me exactly what happened.

00:45.645 --> 00:48.186
♪ I was driving ♪

00:48.187 --> 00:50.826
♪ Had a bit to drink and then
I ran into a milk truck ♪

00:50.827 --> 00:52.230
♪ Yeah-ah ♪

00:52.231 --> 00:53.568
Were you on drugs?

00:53.569 --> 00:55.909
♪ "E" and blow. ♪

00:55.910 --> 00:57.947
Turn that off. I'm mad at TV.

00:57.948 --> 00:59.351
Peter, what's wrong?

00:59.352 --> 01:01.591
Family Guy has been around since 1999

01:01.592 --> 01:04.023
and whenever it's time for the
Emmys, they don't give us one.

01:04.024 --> 01:05.025
I'm sick of it!

01:05.026 --> 01:07.365
Well, I'm not making another
episode with The Simpsons.

01:07.366 --> 01:08.447
What did that get us?

01:08.448 --> 01:09.883
I'll tell you what it got us.

01:09.884 --> 01:11.622
More ink for The Simpsons.

01:11.623 --> 01:14.385
Yeah. "Simpsons plays
down to competition."

01:14.386 --> 01:16.236
"Simpsons step into the sewer."

01:16.237 --> 01:18.275
"Shame on you, Simpsons."

01:18.276 --> 01:20.113
Those lucky bastards.

01:20.114 --> 01:22.301
Well, this week, we do classy comedy.

01:22.302 --> 01:23.424
Emmy comedy.

01:23.425 --> 01:25.263
I think that's a great idea.

01:25.264 --> 01:27.770
It's about time we made
some quality television

01:27.771 --> 01:30.259
like Modern Family,
Girls and Transparent.

01:30.260 --> 01:31.402
That's the spirit.

01:31.403 --> 01:34.524
Griffins, let's make this
our Emmy-winning episode.

01:34.525 --> 01:36.898
So get all your pukes and farts out now.

01:41.177 --> 01:43.250
I mean, I mean, I mean...

01:43.251 --> 01:45.155
not funny.

01:52.929 --> 01:56.389
Kids, it's me, tu madre, Lois Griffin.

01:56.390 --> 01:57.759
Time for breakfast.

01:57.760 --> 01:59.971
Oh, yeah.

01:59.972 --> 02:02.384
Good morning, Lois,
which is who you are.

02:02.385 --> 02:04.554
My wife, Lois. Hugging my wife.

02:08.092 --> 02:10.733
Package for Peter Griffin.

02:10.734 --> 02:12.804
Thank you, unknown delivery woman.

02:12.805 --> 02:14.109
Forget the freaking Emmy.

02:14.110 --> 02:16.275
If you touch her ass, I will...

02:16.276 --> 02:17.986
"Amazon."

02:17.987 --> 02:20.695
Ay, my Uncle Alejandro
lives in the Amazon.

02:20.696 --> 02:24.039
Do you think he has sent us
shoes made from banana leaves?

02:24.040 --> 02:26.212
Boy, the, uh, the ethnic characters

02:26.213 --> 02:27.548
on these Emmy-winning shows

02:27.549 --> 02:29.616
aren't exactly rocket
scientists, are they?

02:29.617 --> 02:32.109
I don't know what you
talkin' about, Liz Lemon.

02:32.110 --> 02:34.422
No, this is something I ordered, for me.

02:37.530 --> 02:39.777
I am a woman and always have been.

02:39.778 --> 02:41.892
I've made plans to undergo surgery

02:41.893 --> 02:44.734
so my wang don't get in the
way of the woman what I am.

02:44.735 --> 02:46.425
Ay, dios mio.

02:46.426 --> 02:48.890
Lois, I'll still be a
parent to our children.

02:48.891 --> 02:51.688
But now I'll be a trans-parent.

02:51.689 --> 02:53.526
Get it? Transparent?

02:53.527 --> 02:54.782
Clever pun, right?

02:56.694 --> 02:58.449
Please, honor me for my courage.

03:05.113 --> 03:07.929
I think gender-reassignment
surgery is very brave

03:07.930 --> 03:09.993
and the fat man should win
some kind of award for it.

03:09.994 --> 03:12.271
- The fat woman.
- He hasn't chopped it off yet.

03:12.272 --> 03:15.073
That doesn't matter. Peter
already identifies as a woman.

03:15.074 --> 03:17.498
And on karaoke night, I
identify as George Michael.

03:17.499 --> 03:19.002
That doesn't mean it's true.

03:19.003 --> 03:21.711
Brian's just mad because
he has to be the lady one.

03:21.712 --> 03:23.703
Which makes you the one
who's gay in real life.

03:24.204 --> 03:27.796
Daddies, I'm standing
here, delivering my line

03:27.797 --> 03:30.364
with more emotion and less of a monotone

03:30.365 --> 03:33.647
than the actual Lily on Modern Family.

03:33.648 --> 03:36.053
I'm now confident enough
to share my truth

03:36.054 --> 03:39.182
with the rest of my loved ones,
beginning with my son, Chris.

03:42.077 --> 03:43.386
Bazinga, Father.

03:43.387 --> 03:46.331
Assuming father is still the
appropriate designation.

03:47.255 --> 03:48.516
What-what are you doing?

03:48.517 --> 03:50.263
Waiting for the laugh to die down.

03:50.264 --> 03:51.767
I'm here because I've decided

03:51.768 --> 03:53.936
to become the woman I am inside.

03:53.937 --> 03:56.482
Can you find it in your
heart to accept me?

03:56.483 --> 03:59.892
Oh, Dad, science has moved so far past

03:59.893 --> 04:01.543
binary gender construction.

04:01.544 --> 04:03.589
And if being a woman makes you happy,

04:03.590 --> 04:06.991
then in the words of Mr.
Spock, "It's only logical."

04:06.992 --> 04:08.785
Wow, I couldn't follow any of that,

04:08.786 --> 04:10.925
but look how smart your audience is.

04:10.926 --> 04:12.982
Ha-ha.

04:18.214 --> 04:20.177
Louis C.K.? Is that you?

04:20.178 --> 04:22.228
Yup. I'm a big fan of yours, Peter.

04:22.229 --> 04:25.250
Wow, that's great because if
Louis C.K. likes something,

04:25.251 --> 04:27.160
- everyone has to.
- That's right.

04:27.161 --> 04:29.848
Well, I'm glad my popularity
has cooled off just enough

04:29.849 --> 04:32.008
that you were able to get me to do this.

04:32.009 --> 04:33.023
Bye, Peter.

04:33.024 --> 04:35.895
Boy, he's not afraid
to go there, I'm told.

04:39.913 --> 04:42.018
- Norm!
- Norm!

04:42.019 --> 04:44.425
Ative gender roles have
been turned upside down.

04:44.426 --> 04:45.928
Correct, Quagmire.

04:45.929 --> 04:47.937
I'm going in for
gender-reassignment surgery.

04:47.938 --> 04:49.005
What the hell, Peter?!

04:49.006 --> 04:50.408
First my dad and now you?

04:50.409 --> 04:52.483
Am-am I... is it... am I
doing this to people?

04:52.484 --> 04:54.789
Is it... do you guys feel like
cutting off your penises?

04:54.790 --> 04:58.934
No, but I can turn it inside out
like rolling up a dress sock.

04:58.935 --> 05:00.739
You guys aren't supporting my choice?

05:00.740 --> 05:02.078
Well, what do you expect, Peter?

05:02.079 --> 05:03.731
I-I mean a sex change operation?

05:03.732 --> 05:04.919
Why are you doing this?

05:04.920 --> 05:06.925
I'll tell you why I'm doing all of this.

05:06.926 --> 05:08.033
For me.

05:08.034 --> 05:10.649
M-E. M-E.

05:10.650 --> 05:13.006
I'm doing it for M-E.

05:18.310 --> 05:20.484
Ew. I mean, yay!

05:26.484 --> 05:30.394
Man or woman, I'm a big fat joke.

05:30.395 --> 05:32.401
No one takes me seriously.

05:32.402 --> 05:34.408
I do, Dad.

05:34.409 --> 05:38.787
You've inspired me to nakedly
eat this cake in a weird place.

05:38.788 --> 05:41.696
Thanks to you, I now believe in me.

05:41.697 --> 05:42.933
Me.

05:42.934 --> 05:44.403
M-E.

05:44.404 --> 05:46.502
I believe in M-E.

05:47.808 --> 05:50.122
Okay, okay, all right.

05:50.123 --> 05:51.778
Don't want one that bad.

05:55.255 --> 05:57.076
Peter, I'd like to introduce the surgeon

05:57.077 --> 05:59.182
who will perform your procedure today.

05:59.183 --> 06:01.254
Dr. Wang Gon.

06:01.255 --> 06:04.364
Wow, I can't believe all you
guys came out to support me.

06:04.365 --> 06:07.005
You guys aren't just the
best friends I've ever had.

06:07.006 --> 06:09.759
You're also the best comedy.

06:09.760 --> 06:11.904
- Aw.
- Aw.

06:14.144 --> 06:15.464
Great job, everyone.

06:15.465 --> 06:17.163
If that don't get us the
Emmy, nothing will.

06:17.164 --> 06:18.705
Where do you think you're going?

06:18.706 --> 06:20.970
Doc, I'm not actually going
through with the operation.

06:20.971 --> 06:22.050
I'm going home.

06:22.051 --> 06:24.324
We're doing this whether
you like it or not.

06:25.762 --> 06:28.168
Doc, no. Stop him! Somebody help!

06:28.169 --> 06:29.907
You want the Emmy, don't you?

06:29.908 --> 06:32.734
And that is how
I became your mother.

06:37.996 --> 06:39.383
So, the Emmy committee

06:39.384 --> 06:40.988
watched our submission for Best Comedy?

06:40.989 --> 06:42.025
Uh-huh.

06:42.591 --> 06:44.163
All right, thank you.

06:44.164 --> 06:46.744
They hated it so much, they
gave us a negative Emmy.

06:46.745 --> 06:48.206
We now owe them an Emmy.

06:49.212 --> 06:50.462
The Emmys aren't fair.

06:50.463 --> 06:53.024
I mean, shows like Nurse
Jackie are basically dramas,

06:53.025 --> 06:54.864
but they get comedy awards all the time.

06:54.865 --> 06:56.366
That's it.

06:56.367 --> 06:58.774
We'll sneak into the drama category.

06:58.775 --> 07:02.453
That's how we'll win the Emmy
with dark, confusing plot twists

07:02.454 --> 07:04.127
like on Homeland or Mad Men.

07:04.128 --> 07:05.962
Ooh, or Breaking Bad.

07:05.963 --> 07:07.667
Or Mr. Robot Chicken.

07:07.668 --> 07:09.506
No, Chris, it's Mr. Robot.

07:09.507 --> 07:11.455
- Chicken.
- Mr. Robot.

07:11.456 --> 07:13.517
- Chicken!
- No, no, Chris, you see,

07:13.518 --> 07:15.758
Mr. Robot is a critically
acclaimed show.

07:15.759 --> 07:19.586
Robot Chicken is something
kids used to watch in 2006.

07:19.587 --> 07:21.509
It's basically four minutes of nonsense

07:21.510 --> 07:24.784
on at 1:00 in the morning
breaking up personal injury ads.

07:25.537 --> 07:26.740
Chicken.

07:42.102 --> 07:44.377
Please, don't.

07:45.346 --> 07:47.788
Why... won't...

07:47.789 --> 07:50.327
you... die?!

07:54.238 --> 07:56.139
_

07:56.140 --> 07:57.551
Shh.

07:57.552 --> 07:59.121
Shh, that's right.

07:59.122 --> 08:00.592
I'm your dad.

08:00.593 --> 08:02.732
Your gentle, suburban dad.

08:02.733 --> 08:05.005
Oh, what a twist. Shh.

08:05.006 --> 08:06.343
Hey, Dad.

08:06.344 --> 08:07.780
Sure must be tough having a son

08:07.781 --> 08:10.121
with goofy noodle legs like mine.

08:10.122 --> 08:11.591
Chris, I love you

08:11.592 --> 08:13.548
no matter how useless you
are in a paddleboat.

08:18.012 --> 08:20.017
Peter, those crows keep getting in.

08:20.018 --> 08:22.123
This whole house is falling apart.

08:22.124 --> 08:25.601
It's okay, my long-suffering,
quietly dissatisfied wife.

08:25.602 --> 08:27.049
We'll get everything repaired.

08:27.050 --> 08:28.746
How? We can't afford it.

08:28.747 --> 08:30.416
We have to pay for Chris's doctor bills

08:30.417 --> 08:32.922
and meds for our daughter in the CIA.

08:36.197 --> 08:37.808
Damn, she's good at her job.

08:37.809 --> 08:39.715
How are we ever gonna
pay all these bills

08:39.716 --> 08:41.413
that have been perfectly
ripped across the top

08:41.414 --> 08:43.752
so the words "past due" are visible?

08:43.753 --> 08:45.092
Oh, I just thank God

08:45.093 --> 08:47.099
there's no devastating
turn of events going on

08:47.100 --> 08:48.870
that I don't know about.

08:51.162 --> 08:52.997
_

08:52.998 --> 08:55.609
- You have cancer.
- How long do I have to live?

08:55.610 --> 08:56.691
One week.

08:56.692 --> 08:58.814
While I give the rest of your diagnosis,

08:58.815 --> 09:00.305
I'm going to gradually talk quieter,

09:00.306 --> 09:01.908
as if I'm growing distant

09:01.909 --> 09:04.649
to show how overwhelmed
you are by this news.

09:25.027 --> 09:27.351
Yo, you five-o?

09:27.352 --> 09:28.989
No, I'm 87.

09:28.990 --> 09:30.595
But how flattering.

09:30.596 --> 09:33.521
Now, get me drugs, scummy drug dealer.

09:33.522 --> 09:36.235
You got it, mayor of our city.

09:38.770 --> 09:42.000
Mm. I wonder which of us
is the bigger criminal.

09:42.001 --> 09:43.070
Oh, that's easy. You are.

09:43.071 --> 09:44.705
Hey, can you teach me to sell drugs?

09:44.706 --> 09:47.378
Hold up. Are you wearing a The Wire?

09:47.379 --> 09:49.651
No. I need money for sympathetic reasons

09:49.652 --> 09:51.558
and I have no other option than crime.

09:51.559 --> 09:54.799
I mean, I could sell stuff
on eBay, but... shipping.

09:54.800 --> 09:57.174
Well, I am pulling a
heist at a meth lab.

09:57.175 --> 09:59.112
I suppose I could use the help.

09:59.113 --> 10:00.907
Great! You won't regret this.

10:00.908 --> 10:02.343
When it comes to selling drugs,

10:02.344 --> 10:03.526
you and me will be a better team

10:03.527 --> 10:05.833
than the old lady's
eyeballs on Downton Abbey.

10:05.834 --> 10:08.977
I'm looking way over in this direction.

10:08.978 --> 10:12.385
And I'm looking way over here.

10:12.386 --> 10:15.796
That way we can see all
the awards flying at us.

10:15.797 --> 10:18.003
Here comes one now.

10:18.004 --> 10:20.878
Best Cutaway.

10:30.056 --> 10:32.780
Remember, kill anything that moves.

10:32.781 --> 10:34.919
- Even a kid?
- Especially a kid.

10:34.920 --> 10:37.795
You got to kill a kid at least
once a season to make people go,

10:37.796 --> 10:40.303
"Oh, I can't believe they killed a kid."

10:40.304 --> 10:42.041
Let's go.

10:45.370 --> 10:47.440
_

10:48.287 --> 10:49.546
Wait, we did this already.

10:49.547 --> 10:50.753
G-Go back.

10:50.754 --> 10:52.157
Or-Or forward?

10:52.158 --> 10:53.480
I'm-I'm lost.

10:53.481 --> 10:55.420
_

11:10.827 --> 11:12.316
I'll get help!

11:19.169 --> 11:21.694
Brian, call off
this drone strike,

11:21.695 --> 11:23.064
Dad needs us.

11:23.065 --> 11:25.404
Damn it, Meg, we're about to
take out the head of ISIS!

11:25.405 --> 11:27.042
Hoo! Woo-hoo! Woo-hoo! Woo-hoo!

11:27.043 --> 11:28.949
Woo-hoo! Woo-hoo! Woo-hoo!
Woo-hoo! Woo-hoo!

11:28.950 --> 11:31.055
- Woo-hoo! Woo-hoo! Woo-hoo!
- Okay, you've made your point.

11:31.056 --> 11:33.395
You're lucky you're so good at your job.

11:33.396 --> 11:34.918
Wha...?

11:59.157 --> 12:01.847
That was badass how it went
from the guy burning up

12:01.848 --> 12:04.222
to the barbecue, right? Best Director.

12:04.223 --> 12:06.293
Hey, Peter, I was thinking
about this Emmy thing.

12:06.294 --> 12:08.735
What's the most acclaimed
drama of all time?

12:08.736 --> 12:10.004
- The Sopranos.
- Right.

12:10.005 --> 12:11.324
And what's the most memorable moment

12:11.325 --> 12:14.188
- in the history of that show?
- Well, I'd have to say...

12:27.808 --> 12:29.823
Nice briefcase full of cash.

12:31.118 --> 12:33.742
Where'd you get the money for
a briefcase like that, Peter?

12:33.743 --> 12:35.089
I want in.

12:35.090 --> 12:38.715
I need the money to pay off my
mysterious boss, Mr. Robot.

12:38.716 --> 12:39.891
Chicken!

12:39.892 --> 12:41.350
Chris, get back in the house!

12:42.786 --> 12:44.475
My whole plan,

12:44.476 --> 12:47.818
fallin' apart like a... House of Cards.

12:47.819 --> 12:49.756
You know, growing up in Gaffney,

12:49.757 --> 12:52.330
my daddy always said,
"Turn the other cheek."

12:52.331 --> 12:54.303
Kevin Spacey always said,

12:54.304 --> 12:57.279
"I was just walkin' my dog
in that park at 3:00 a.m."

12:57.280 --> 12:59.119
I don't trust either one of 'em.

12:59.120 --> 13:01.997
I suppose it's time to
tell my wife the truth.

13:01.998 --> 13:03.664
Like a man.

13:05.570 --> 13:08.479
And then, I
sold all the drugs...

13:08.480 --> 13:11.523
'cause the doctor said
I had the cancer...

13:11.524 --> 13:13.026
and I killed the guys,

13:13.027 --> 13:15.533
and Joe took all the mon... the money!

13:17.841 --> 13:19.731
I see.

13:21.436 --> 13:23.190
Are... are you leavin' me?

13:23.191 --> 13:24.561
No, Peter.

13:24.562 --> 13:26.900
I'm helping you kill that cop.

13:26.901 --> 13:30.497
Because I'm darker than you and
the audience ever thought!

13:30.498 --> 13:32.051
What a twist.

13:32.052 --> 13:35.326
For five long years,
orange was my new black.

13:37.802 --> 13:40.073
Peter, I don't care if it's drug money.

13:40.074 --> 13:41.845
I have grown accustomed to Hulu Plus.

13:41.846 --> 13:44.354
If you think I'm going back to
regular Hulu, you're crazy!

13:44.355 --> 13:45.924
We don't even watch that much Hulu.

13:45.925 --> 13:47.831
I still want it just in case!

13:47.832 --> 13:50.438
Now take off all your clothes
so we don't get blood on 'em...

13:50.439 --> 13:53.115
when we kill that cop in the desert.

13:53.116 --> 13:56.102
Oh, the beginning all makes sense now.

13:56.744 --> 13:59.159
_

13:59.160 --> 14:01.367
_

14:01.368 --> 14:03.225
_

14:07.253 --> 14:12.856
Why... won't... you... die?!

14:42.811 --> 14:44.098
Whoa!

14:44.099 --> 14:46.004
I did not see that coming.

14:46.005 --> 14:47.542
One more. Let's watch one more.

14:47.543 --> 14:48.979
Well, hold on.

14:48.980 --> 14:50.350
Like all television viewers,

14:50.351 --> 14:51.955
our first priority before deciding

14:51.956 --> 14:53.360
to continue watching a show

14:53.361 --> 14:55.632
should be whether or not it
features enough diversity.

14:55.633 --> 14:57.505
I felt very well-represented.

14:57.506 --> 14:59.076
Aw, I'm glad, honey.

14:59.077 --> 15:00.546
Mmm.

15:00.547 --> 15:02.939
Hey, thanks for letting
me come over, you guys.

15:10.291 --> 15:11.845
Telegram for Mr. Griffin.

15:11.846 --> 15:13.215
Thank you, someone's nephew.

15:13.216 --> 15:14.519
Would you mind reading it out loud

15:14.520 --> 15:16.223
for maximum old-timey effect?

15:16.224 --> 15:19.065
"To P. Griffin, from the
Emmy Board of Governors.

15:19.066 --> 15:20.704
Dear Mr. Griffin, stop.

15:20.705 --> 15:22.977
We understand you've been
attempting to win an Emmy, stop.

15:22.978 --> 15:25.051
- Stop, stop."
- Is that all?

15:25.052 --> 15:26.899
No, there's another from Fleetwood Mac.

15:26.900 --> 15:29.264
"Don't stop, stop.
Thinking about tomorrow, stop."

15:29.265 --> 15:30.666
And here's one from The Supremes.

15:30.667 --> 15:32.666
"Stop, stop. In the name of love, stop."

15:32.667 --> 15:34.981
- Are you finished?
- Are you asking me to stop, stop?

15:34.982 --> 15:36.952
Peter, close the door.

15:36.953 --> 15:38.357
Well, that's it.

15:38.358 --> 15:39.794
We didn't get Best Drama either.

15:39.795 --> 15:42.335
This is hopeless. We've
tried everything.

15:43.184 --> 15:44.944
No, Lois, we haven't.

15:44.945 --> 15:48.186
But that's just what we're
gonna do... Everything!

15:48.187 --> 15:51.062
We're gonna try for every
single Emmy category.

15:51.063 --> 15:53.134
Starting with Best Stunt Performance.

15:53.135 --> 15:55.207
Aah!

15:55.208 --> 15:56.677
Peter, I don't think that's a category.

15:56.678 --> 15:58.049
Oh, okay.

15:58.050 --> 15:59.989
Best Documentary.

15:59.990 --> 16:01.358
Aah!

16:09.232 --> 16:11.288
Chris
is playing my dummy nephew.

16:11.289 --> 16:13.896
Our family actually lines
up really well for this.

16:13.897 --> 16:15.801
Best Competitive Reality Show!

16:21.838 --> 16:24.094
- Peter, you're out.
- I'm off the show?

16:24.095 --> 16:25.796
No, your penis is out.

16:25.797 --> 16:27.098
- You're in.
- I'm in?

16:27.099 --> 16:29.435
No, urine is running down your leg.

16:29.436 --> 16:32.285
Outstanding Casting for a Comedy Series!

16:32.286 --> 16:34.959
Okay, so the deal is,
I get girls like you jobs.

16:34.960 --> 16:37.267
The jobs pay $1,000 to $5,000 a day.

16:37.268 --> 16:38.671
I'm recording this interview.

16:38.672 --> 16:40.543
And then I send the
demo tape to producers,

16:40.544 --> 16:41.980
and if they like you,
they're gonna hire you.

16:41.981 --> 16:43.780
Have you done anything like this before?

16:43.781 --> 16:45.859
Never. This is my first time.

16:45.860 --> 16:47.497
All right, now, a lot of
these scenes are gonna be

16:47.498 --> 16:49.302
you interacting with someone else,

16:49.303 --> 16:51.174
so I'll just come around
and read with you.

16:51.175 --> 16:52.579
Now, since I'm holding the camera,

16:52.580 --> 16:55.086
I'm gonna need some help
with my belt buckle.

16:55.087 --> 16:58.028
And there you have it,
Family Guy reaches a new low

16:58.029 --> 17:01.338
as it grovels and begs
for a meaningless award.

17:01.339 --> 17:03.577
I would say they've got about as
much chance of winning an Emmy

17:03.579 --> 17:07.256
as the Republican Party has
of accomplishing something.

17:09.128 --> 17:10.585
Peter, over here.

17:16.769 --> 17:20.295
Bill Maher? What are you doing
not smirking outside a church?

17:20.296 --> 17:21.599
Uh, yeah, I was just doing that.

17:21.600 --> 17:23.905
Uh, look, Peter, I'm
here for two reasons:

17:23.906 --> 17:26.880
first, to find out who that
Asian girl was on the couch,

17:26.881 --> 17:28.485
and second, to tell you that

17:28.486 --> 17:32.364
Family Guy will never, ever win an Emmy.

17:32.365 --> 17:33.768
Okay, first of all, that was Asa Akira.

17:33.769 --> 17:35.173
I think you knew that.

17:35.174 --> 17:37.847
Second, are you sayin' there's
a conspiracy against us?

17:37.848 --> 17:39.804
Follow the Emmy.

17:54.999 --> 17:56.736
It's back this way.

17:56.737 --> 17:59.177
And who was that Asian
girl on the couch?

17:59.178 --> 18:00.868
I think you knew who that was.

18:08.533 --> 18:10.537
_

18:11.231 --> 18:14.757
_

18:19.589 --> 18:21.176
To convey this moment of shock

18:21.177 --> 18:23.149
at the depth of the
conspiracy around me,

18:23.150 --> 18:26.426
here's Ryan O'Neal in the
movie Tough Guys Don't Dance.

18:26.427 --> 18:28.832
Oh, man.

18:28.833 --> 18:30.304
Oh, God. Oh, man.

18:30.305 --> 18:31.641
Oh, God.

18:31.642 --> 18:33.045
Oh, man.

18:33.046 --> 18:34.986
Oh, God. Oh, man.

18:34.987 --> 18:37.693
Oh, God. Oh, man. Oh, God!

18:42.810 --> 18:44.016
Peter, there you are.

18:44.017 --> 18:45.454
I've been calling you all night.

18:45.455 --> 18:46.736
Where the hell have you been?

18:46.737 --> 18:47.759
No time to explain.

18:47.760 --> 18:49.495
This Emmy thing goes deep.

18:49.496 --> 18:51.901
The same people win year
after year after year.

18:51.902 --> 18:54.509
It's like there's some
kind of secret society

18:54.510 --> 18:56.950
that takes all the awards and
is keepin' us from getting one.

18:56.951 --> 18:59.142
Yeah, I know. They're
all here to see you.

19:00.411 --> 19:01.965
Hello, Peter.

19:01.966 --> 19:03.269
The Michelin Man?

19:03.270 --> 19:04.384
You're part of this?

19:04.385 --> 19:07.749
No, I'm two-time
Emmy-winner Alec Baldwin.

19:07.750 --> 19:09.856
Peter, stop snooping around the Emmys.

19:09.857 --> 19:12.095
Yeah, butt out. It's
none of your business.

19:12.096 --> 19:13.865
Well, why not, Julie Bowen?

19:13.866 --> 19:15.941
Huge fan, by the way. Just huge.

19:15.942 --> 19:17.164
What are you hiding?

19:17.165 --> 19:18.615
What's the big, secret reason

19:18.616 --> 19:20.163
Family Guy can't win an Emmy?

19:22.779 --> 19:24.432
All right, we'll tell you.

19:24.433 --> 19:26.438
Your show sucks.

19:26.439 --> 19:28.612
Peter, I'm famous writer Aaron Sorkin.

19:28.613 --> 19:29.808
Walk and talk with me.

19:29.809 --> 19:31.454
You wouldn't know my work because

19:31.455 --> 19:33.160
I don't write for Juggs magazine.

19:33.161 --> 19:35.298
Let me explain "writing" to you.

19:35.299 --> 19:37.170
You can't take a scene
from Ferris Bueller,

19:37.171 --> 19:39.878
cross out the name "Ferris,"
and replace it with "Peter."

19:39.879 --> 19:43.255
And the racial stuff on your
show is just embarrassing.

19:43.256 --> 19:45.930
You have people of color
voiced by white actors.

19:45.931 --> 19:47.601
- No!
- Yes!

19:47.602 --> 19:49.172
Hell, I'm Shonda Rhimes,

19:49.173 --> 19:51.446
and I'm being voiced by a white actor.

19:51.447 --> 19:52.716
And worst of all,

19:52.717 --> 19:55.391
you take this big pile of garbage,

19:55.392 --> 19:58.702
and you tie it all up by having
everyone sit around saying,

19:58.703 --> 20:00.808
"At least everything's back to normal,"

20:00.809 --> 20:02.646
as if something happened.

20:02.647 --> 20:04.452
When nothing happened!

20:04.453 --> 20:07.393
It was a complete waste
of everyone's time!

20:13.864 --> 20:16.020
Well, I'm glad all this
Emmy nonsense is over

20:16.021 --> 20:17.457
and things are back to normal.

20:17.458 --> 20:18.929
Yeah, me, too.

20:18.930 --> 20:20.466
You know, I may not get Emmys,

20:20.467 --> 20:23.919
but I do get the best award
of all... My family.

20:23.920 --> 20:25.977
And this e-mail from a young fan.

20:25.978 --> 20:27.654
"Dear sir, your show helped me

20:27.655 --> 20:29.910
when I was going through chemotherapy."

20:29.911 --> 20:31.065
Aw.

20:31.066 --> 20:34.174
"My favorite episode was when
Homer stays home from church..."

20:34.175 --> 20:35.911
Ah, damn it, he thinks
we're The Simpsons.

20:35.912 --> 20:38.051
Hey, what do you say, one last try?

20:38.052 --> 20:39.174
Why not?

20:39.175 --> 20:40.308
Ladies and gentlemen,

20:40.309 --> 20:43.736
please enjoy this spectacular,
live-action chicken fight,

20:43.737 --> 20:45.106
starring Ty Burrell.

20:45.107 --> 20:46.276
Good night!

20:48.685 --> 20:51.225
Shh. Shh.

20:55.203 --> 20:56.760
I don't have any more room in my house.

20:56.761 --> 21:02.004
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru